course: dictionary
lesson: 3842
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer means. The word forum has three main meanings, so look at the clues around it to choose the right one.
explain: «The Romans wrote their laws on twelve tablets displayed in the forum.» Here a forum is a public square in ancient Rome where people gathered. The clue is displayed: the tablets were shown in a place where everyone could see them.
explain: «Forum posts with no name» means something different. A forum can also be an online message board where people post questions and answers. The clue is posts. Remember that you should never share personal details on public forums.
fact: A forum is a place, meeting or website where people discuss a topic and share views.
fact: An online forum is a message board where people post questions and answers.
fact: In ancient Rome, the forum was the main public square for markets, meetings and speeches.
fact: «The forum was the centre of a Roman town, with markets, temples, law courts and speeches.»
fact: The plural of forum can be forums or fora.
exercise: «The town centre was the forum, where people shopped, did business and listened to speeches.» What does forum mean here? | *A public square where people shopped and met | A type of boat | A kind of school exam | An online message board
exercise: «Forum posts with no name» suggests what? | *Messages put online by people who did not give their name | Posts written on paper in a Roman square | Pictures painted on a wall | Letters sent by post with a stamp
exercise: «The forum was the centre of a Roman town, with markets, temples, law courts and speeches.» Find and copy the words that name a place where justice was decided. | temples | *law courts | markets | speeches
test: Which safe choice should you make when using a public forum? | *Keep your name, address and school private | Post a photo of your school uniform | Share your address so friends can find you | Tell everyone your password
test: Which sentence uses forum as an online message board? | The Romans displayed their laws in the forum | *Someone asked a question on the forum and got three answers | The town centre was the forum | The forum was a centre with temples and markets
exam: Ella reads «The forum was the centre of a Roman town, with markets and speeches.» Which meaning fits, and what is the clue? | A kind of school exam, because of the clue speeches | An online message board, because of the clue centre | *A public square in ancient Rome, because of the clue Roman town | A type of boat, because of the clue markets
